  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ILO SCORE phase IV</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The program provides training to local businesses for improving their productivity, competitiveness and working conditions through five training modules that include workplace cooperation, quality management, clean production, human resource management and occupational safety and health. Phase IV will extend activities in the four countries where implementation was launched most recently, i.e. Bolivia, Ethiopia, Myanmar, and Tunisia. The Gender Equality module of the SCORE training focuses on five key issues: voice equality, inclusive hiring, equal pay for work of equal value, work climate, and work-life harmony. It consists of an eight-month training and coaching process tailored to the specific needs of the SME and its workers. The module was designed specifically with the management and financial capacities of SMEs in mind. It provides concrete training and counselling for the implementation of best management practices in gender equality, to support better working conditions for women and men, and improve enterprise productivity.</narrative>
  </description>
